{"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"A handle that identifies one entity in a world.","type":"text"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/worldmodule\/entity"]}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"relationshipsSections":[{"kind":"relationships","identifiers":["doc:\/\/WorldModule\/s15BitwiseCopyableP","doc:\/\/WorldModule\/SL","doc:\/\/WorldModule\/s8CopyableP","doc:\/\/WorldModule\/s23CustomStringConvertibleP","doc:\/\/WorldModule\/Se","doc:\/\/WorldModule\/SE","doc:\/\/WorldModule\/SQ","doc:\/\/WorldModule\/s9EscapableP","doc:\/\/WorldModule\/SH","doc:\/\/WorldModule\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/WorldModule\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"title":"Conforms To","type":"conformsTo"}],"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule"]]},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Entity"},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"@frozen","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Entity","kind":"identifier"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","anchor":"overview","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"An entity is one thing in your game or simulation. It has no data of its own: a ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/World","type":"reference"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"stores the components it holds, and the handle is how you refer to it. You get a handle by","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"spawning an entity, and you pass it back to the world to read and change its components:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["var world = World()","let hero = world.spawn(Name(value: \"Ada\"), Health(current: 100))","","print(world[Name.self, of: hero].value)","\/\/ Prints \"Ada\""],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A handle is a small value, cheap to copy and store, for example in a component that refers to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"another entity. It holds two numbers: the "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Entity\/index","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" of the slot the entity occupies in the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"world, and the "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Entity\/generation","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" of that slot. When an entity is despawned, the world can reuse"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"its slot for a new entity with the next generation, so a handle kept past its entity’s despawn"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"stale"}]},{"type":"text","text":": it never names the entity that took the slot."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["var world = World()","let first = world.spawn(Position(x: 0, y: 0))","world.despawn(first)","let second = world.spawn(Position(x: 1, y: 1))","","print(first, second)","\/\/ Prints \"0:0 0:1\"","print(world.contains(first))","\/\/ Prints \"false\""],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Entities are ordered by slot, then by generation."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Operators","identifiers":["doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Entity\/_(_:_:)"],"title":"Operators","generated":true},{"anchor":"Initializers","identifiers":["doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Entity\/init(from:)","doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Entity\/init(index:generation:)"],"title":"Initializers","generated":true},{"anchor":"Instance-Properties","identifiers":["doc:\/\/WorldModule\/d